+\section{Sensor Fusion and Score Evidence}
+Fusion is the bridge between the radar paper and the EI result. The accepted prior-fusion comparator combines radar/cue branches through a human-engineered late-fusion score, train/CV threshold selection, and the same blind-holdout protocol. EI then operates on the detector-view score surface rather than on forbidden generator internals. It searches candidate component families on train/CV rows, optimizes sparse nonnegative weights, calibrates monotonically, writes a selection lock, and only then scores the blind holdout.
+
+Figure~\ref{fig:kpiladder} is the familiar ladder view: individual branches first, accepted prior fusion second, and EI last. This makes the claim visually harder to misunderstand. The fusion baseline is already stronger than any single classical branch at the primary operating point, and EI is evaluated as an incremental challenger on top of the same evidence contract.
